<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ligdan Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1588">1588</a>–1634</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ligdan Khan was the last great khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-yuan">Northern Yuan</a>, ruling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chahar-mongols">Chahar Mongols</a> from 1604. He tried to restore central authority over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> by force and patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhism</a>, sponsoring a Mongolian translation of the Kanjur. Defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> Later Jin, he fled west and died in 1634, and his son surrendered the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ligdan-khan.jpg" alt="Ligdan Khan" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avishay · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LIGDEN_HUTAGT_KHAN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
